    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0232" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/810.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Great
                            Britain to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-21T16:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1912—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Government have instructed their Minister in Peking to cooperate with
                    his interested colleagues in protesting vigorously <pb facs="0233" n="117"
                        xml:id="pg117"/> against the reported Belgian loan, discussed in your
                    telegraphic instruction of March 19, 7 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reid.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
